{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "Canonical genre/mood/geography/attribute vocabulary for genre aggregation.",
    "",
    "This file is the SHIPPED DEFAULT. A user's edits from the Config page are written",
    "to <config_dir>/genre_vocabulary.json and take precedence, so a repo update never",
    "clobbers them. The Config page offers a reset back to this file.",
    "",
    "Entry shape:",
    "  id           stable canonical identity, never a display string (snake_case)",
    "  display      what gets written to the file tags",
    "  parent       id of the immediate broader genre, or null for a family root",
    "  specificity  0 family root, 1 broad, 2 established subgenre, 3 narrow/microgenre",
    "  aliases      EXTRA spellings only - the lowercased display name and the",
    "               id-with-spaces are derived automatically, so do not repeat them",
    "  family       hierarchy branch used for the family-slot limit; defaults to the",
    "               root ancestor's id when omitted",
    "",
    "Adding an entry is enough to make it selectable; nothing is hardcoded in Python."
  ],

